          <Pad Id="OwxVPvm46RRDVgEJkuoW2M" Bounds="-620,-60,540,1100" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="03 - In or out.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Move the mouse across the shape in the renderer. Inside, the fill appears and CONTAINS&#xD;&#xA;flips to true. That flip - a question about space, answered every frame - is the whole&#xD;&#xA;chapter.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE SHAPE IS CONCAVE ON PURPOSE. Trace the notch at its top right: the cursor can be&#xD;&#xA;close, surrounded by the shape on two sides, and still OUTSIDE. Near is a feeling.&#xD;&#xA;Inside is a fact with a definition, and the polygon knows the definition.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TWO NODES, ONE QUESTION:&#xD;&#xA;  Contains (A, B)    does A contain B?    the polygon goes first&#xD;&#xA;  Within (A, B)      is A within B?       the point goes first&#xD;&#xA;They always agree. Both exist so your patch can read left to right whichever way the&#xD;&#xA;data flows - swapping two links to change the question is easy to misread later.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;PLAY&#xD;&#xA;  Trace the boundary slowly. The exact edge counts as OUTSIDE - Contains excludes a&#xD;&#xA;  point lying exactly on the boundary. The node's own tooltip names Covers as the&#xD;&#xA;  version without that exception.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  Reshape the polygon - the six corners are pads like any others. Make the notch&#xD;&#xA;  deeper. Cut a second one.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;  Wire Contains somewhere else: the cursor dot's Radius, a sound, anything. An answer&#xD;&#xA;  that updates every frame is a signal, and that is the difference between this and a&#xD;&#xA;  desktop GIS.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT HAPPENED?&#xD;&#xA;  You asked a question about two geometries and watched the answer change. GIS calls&#xD;&#xA;  these questions SPATIAL PREDICATES, and there is a family of them - Intersects ships&#xD;&#xA;  already; Touches, Overlaps and Crosses are on VL.NetTopologySuite's roadmap, arriving&#xD;&#xA;  as chapters need them.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;GIS WORDS&#xD;&#xA;  spatial predicate   a yes/no question about how two geometries relate&#xD;&#xA;  Contains / Within   the same containment, named from either end&#xD;&#xA;  boundary            the edge itself - which Contains does not count as inside&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;CREATIVE CONNECTION&#xD;&#xA;  This is a hit test - collision detection, which you have written a hundred times.&#xD;&#xA;  GIS gives it a rigorous definition, a vocabulary, and sixty answers a second.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THIS PATCH USES ONE PACKAGE, VL.NetTopologySuite, which is normally a reason to live in&#xD;&#xA;that package's own help folder rather than here. It is the exemption written into this&#xD;&#xA;pack's rules: the geometry act runs on that package alone, and a course with a hole in&#xD;&#xA;its opening act is worse than a node appearing in two places.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;NEXT - three directions, no order:&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 04             how far, exactly - distance as a drawable line&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 02             where these shapes came from&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 06             the earth, when you are ready for it">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
        </Canvas>
